WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
Sam knows the verb
for "to play": jugar.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.330
In the past, it takes regular endings.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.690
For "I played football
yesterday" he writes:

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.550
Ayer jugé al fútbol.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.650
His friend Pablo corrects
him: Ayer jugué al fútbol.

6
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.610
Pablo has slipped in an
extra letter: the letter u.

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.370
If the verb is regular, why
would it need an extra letter?

8
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.170
In this mission, you'll find
the verbs that change their

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.350
spelling in the "I" form only,
and the reason they do it.

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.930
Then you'll meet verbs that swap
a vowel, but only for "he",

11
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.970
"she" and "they": durmió, pidió.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.210
Finally, you'll sort regular
verbs from irregular ones.

13
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.540
Your mission: work out why
Pablo added the letter u.
